I was only tentatively attempting a genocide-less ascension, but much of
the temptation was removed when I lost my BoH after a nasty
Asmodeus/Yeenoghu/fooLich-summoning-storm/mindflayer encounter that
resulted in a lot of forgotten levels and items.  I also lost a 1:2 wand of
wishing in the blast, and several candles (I don't think I ever found seven
of these though.)

I made a number of other dumb mistakes, such as donning an un-id'ed helmet,
instantly losing 10 points of protection ("Hey, I've got lots of holy
water, what's the worst that can happen if I try on this un-id'ed helm?", I
thought smugly to myself...), and blowing up a +5 cloak of displacement
when I read the wrong scroll.

I still had a magic lamp, and when I found another in Vlad's tower I used
it to get my candles, and then wasted my first one on a new BoH.

One lucky break I had:  smoky potions were full-healing, and I got two
wishes from this after some alchemy.

Never having done genoless before, I found that:
- Liches were less annoying than I expected once I became powerful enough
- Mind Flayers are a bloody PITA, best to be avoided completely if you
  don't have good ranged weapons.
- Don't whack the Disenchanter, son.  With your AC, it's much less likely
  to do you harm even if it's standing beside you and you can't move (at
  least, that was my perception.  No idea what the actual statistics are.)

I got GDSM early on due to another lucky wish (don't remember how), and the
only /oPoly and !oPoly that I may have had got blown up, so I also mostly
inadvertently managed to get polyless and "you never changed form"
conducts.



